---Contains information about a contact.
---@class aws.connect.Contact
---@field Arn? aws.connect.ARN The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the contact.
---@field Id? aws.connect.ContactId The identifier for the contact.
---@field InitialContactId? aws.connect.ContactId If this contact is related to other contacts, this is the ID of the initial contact.
---@field PreviousContactId? aws.connect.ContactId If this contact is not the first contact, this is the ID of the previous contact.
---@field ContactAssociationId? aws.connect.ContactId This is the root contactId which is used as a unique identifier for all subsequent contacts in a contact tree.
---@field InitiationMethod? aws.connect.ContactInitiationMethod Indicates how the contact was initiated.
---@field Name? distilled.Secret The name of the contact.
---@field Description? distilled.Secret The description of the contact.
---@field Channel? aws.connect.Channel How the contact reached your contact center.
---@field QueueInfo? aws.connect.QueueInfo If this contact was queued, this contains information about the queue.
---@field AgentInfo? aws.connect.AgentInfo Information about the agent who accepted the contact.
---@field InitiationTimestamp? aws.connect.Timestamp The date and time this contact was initiated, in UTC time. For INBOUND, this is when the contact arrived. For OUTBOUND, this is when the agent began dialing. For CALLBACK, this is when the callback contact was created. For TRANSFER and QUEUE_TRANSFER, this is when the transfer was initiated. For API, this is when the request arrived. For EXTERNAL_OUTBOUND, this is when the agent started dialing th...
---@field DisconnectTimestamp? aws.connect.Timestamp The date and time that the customer endpoint disconnected from the current contact, in UTC time. In transfer scenarios, the DisconnectTimestamp of the previous contact indicates the date and time when that contact ended.
---@field LastUpdateTimestamp? aws.connect.Timestamp The timestamp when contact was last updated.
---@field LastPausedTimestamp? aws.connect.Timestamp The timestamp when the contact was last paused.
---@field LastResumedTimestamp? aws.connect.Timestamp The timestamp when the contact was last resumed.
---@field RingStartTimestamp? aws.connect.Timestamp The timestamp when ringing started for a campaign call.
---@field TotalPauseCount? aws.connect.TotalPauseCount Total pause count for a contact.
---@field TotalPauseDurationInSeconds? aws.connect.TotalPauseDurationInSeconds Total pause duration for a contact in seconds.
---@field ScheduledTimestamp? aws.connect.Timestamp The timestamp, in Unix epoch time format, at which to start running the inbound flow.
---@field RelatedContactId? aws.connect.ContactId The contactId that is related to this contact.
---@field WisdomInfo? aws.connect.WisdomInfo Information about Connect Customer Wisdom.
---@field CustomerId? aws.connect.CustomerId The customer's identification number. For example, the CustomerId may be a customer number from your CRM. You can create a Lambda function to pull the unique customer ID of the caller from your CRM system. If you enable Connect Customer Voice ID capability, this attribute is populated with the CustomerSpeakerId of the caller.
---@field CustomerEndpoint? aws.connect.EndpointInfo The customer or external third party participant endpoint.
---@field SystemEndpoint? aws.connect.EndpointInfo The system endpoint. For INBOUND, this is the phone number or email address that the customer dialed. For OUTBOUND and EXTERNAL_OUTBOUND, this is the outbound caller ID number assigned to the outbound queue that is used to dial the customer. For callback, this shows up as Softphone for calls handled by agents with softphone.
---@field QueueTimeAdjustmentSeconds? aws.connect.QueueTimeAdjustmentSeconds An integer that represents the queue time adjust to be applied to the contact, in seconds (longer / larger queue time are routed preferentially). Cannot be specified if the QueuePriority is specified. Must be statically defined and a valid integer value.
---@field QueuePriority? aws.connect.QueuePriority An integer that represents the queue priority to be applied to the contact (lower priorities are routed preferentially). Cannot be specified if the QueueTimeAdjustmentSeconds is specified. Must be statically defined, must be larger than zero, and a valid integer value. Default Value is 5.
---@field Tags? aws.connect.ContactTagMap Tags associated with the contact. This contains both Amazon Web Services generated and user-defined tags.
---@field ConnectedToSystemTimestamp? aws.connect.Timestamp The timestamp when customer endpoint connected to Connect Customer.
---@field RoutingCriteria? aws.connect.RoutingCriteria Latest routing criteria on the contact.
---@field Customer? aws.connect.Customer Information about the Customer on the contact.
---@field Campaign? aws.connect.Campaign
---@field AnsweringMachineDetectionStatus? aws.connect.AnsweringMachineDetectionStatus Indicates how an outbound campaign call is actually disposed if the contact is connected to Connect Customer.
---@field CustomerVoiceActivity? aws.connect.CustomerVoiceActivity Information about customer’s voice activity.
---@field QualityMetrics? aws.connect.QualityMetrics Information about the quality of the participant's media connection.
---@field ChatMetrics? aws.connect.ChatMetrics Information about how agent, bot, and customer interact in a chat contact.
---@field DisconnectDetails? aws.connect.DisconnectDetails Information about the call disconnect experience.
---@field AdditionalEmailRecipients? aws.connect.AdditionalEmailRecipients List of additional email addresses for an email contact.
---@field SegmentAttributes? aws.connect.SegmentAttributes A set of system defined key-value pairs stored on individual contact segments using an attribute map. The attributes are standard Connect Customer attributes and can be accessed in flows. Attribute keys can include only alphanumeric, -, and _ characters. This field can be used to show channel subtype. For example, connect:Guide or connect:SMS.
---@field Recordings? aws.connect.Recordings If recording was enabled, this is information about the recordings.
---@field DisconnectReason? aws.connect.String The disconnect reason for the contact. For a list and description of all the possible disconnect reasons by channel, see DisconnectReason under ContactTraceRecord in the Connect Customer Administrator Guide.
---@field ContactEvaluations? aws.connect.ContactEvaluations Information about the contact evaluations where the key is the FormId, which is a unique identifier for the form.
---@field TaskTemplateInfo? aws.connect.TaskTemplateInfoV2 If this contact was created using a task template, this contains information about the task template.
---@field Cases? aws.connect.CaseEntries A list of cases associated with the contact. This field is populated when one or more cases have been linked to the contact.
---@field ContactDetails? aws.connect.ContactDetails A map of string key/value pairs that contain user-defined attributes which are lightly typed within the contact. This object is used only for task contacts.
---@field OutboundStrategy? aws.connect.OutboundStrategy Information about the outbound strategy.
---@field Attributes? aws.connect.Attributes The attributes of the contact.
---@field NextContacts? aws.connect.NextContacts List of next contact entries for the contact.
---@field GlobalResiliencyMetadata? aws.connect.GlobalResiliencyMetadata Information about the global resiliency configuration for the contact, including traffic distribution details.
---@field ContactLens? aws.connect.ContactLens Information about the conversational analytics configuration applied to the contact. This field is present only for contacts where conversational analytics is enabled in the contact flow.

