---@class aws.connect.CreateDataTableAttributeRequest
---@field InstanceId aws.connect.InstanceId The unique identifier for the Amazon Connect instance.
---@field DataTableId aws.connect.DataTableId The unique identifier for the data table. Must also accept the table ARN with or without a version alias. If the version is provided as part of the identifier or ARN, the version must be one of the two available system managed aliases, $SAVED or $LATEST.
---@field Name aws.connect.DataTableName The name for the attribute. Must conform to Connect human readable string specification and have 1-127 characters. Must not start with the reserved case insensitive values 'connect:' and 'aws:'. Whitespace trimmed before persisting. Must be unique for the data table using case-insensitive comparison.
---@field ValueType aws.connect.DataTableAttributeValueType|string The type of value allowed or the resultant type after the value's expression is evaluated. Must be one of TEXT, TEXT_LIST, NUMBER, NUMBER_LIST, and BOOLEAN.
---@field Description? aws.connect.DataTableDescription An optional description for the attribute. Must conform to Connect human readable string specification and have 0-250 characters. Whitespace trimmed before persisting.
---@field Primary? aws.connect.Boolean Optional boolean that defaults to false. Determines if the value is used to identify a record in the table. Values for primary attributes must not be expressions.
---@field Validation? aws.connect.Validation Optional validation rules for the attribute. Borrows heavily from JSON Schema - Draft 2020-12. The maximum length of arrays within validations and depth of validations is 5. There are default limits that apply to all types. Customer specified limits in excess of the default limits are not permitted.

---@class aws.connect.CreateDataTableAttributeResponse
---@field Name aws.connect.DataTableName The name of the created attribute since it also serves as the identifier. This could be different than the parameter passed in since it will be trimmed for whitespace.
---@field AttributeId? aws.connect.DataTableId The unique identifier assigned to the created attribute.
---@field LockVersion aws.connect.DataTableLockVersion The lock version information for the data table and attribute, used for optimistic locking and versioning.

---@class aws.connect.CreateDataTableRequest
---@field InstanceId aws.connect.InstanceId The unique identifier for the Amazon Connect instance where the data table will be created.
---@field Name aws.connect.DataTableName The name for the data table. Must conform to Connect human readable string specification and have 1-127 characters. Whitespace must be trimmed first. Must not start with the reserved case insensitive values 'connect:' and 'aws:'. Must be unique for the instance using case-insensitive comparison.
---@field Description? aws.connect.DataTableDescription An optional description for the data table. Must conform to Connect human readable string specification and have 0-250 characters. Whitespace must be trimmed first.
---@field TimeZone aws.connect.TimeZone The IANA timezone identifier to use when resolving time based dynamic values. Required even if no time slices are specified.
---@field ValueLockLevel aws.connect.DataTableLockLevel|string The data level that concurrent value edits are locked on. One of DATA_TABLE, PRIMARY_VALUE, ATTRIBUTE, VALUE, and NONE. NONE is the default if unspecified. This determines how concurrent edits are handled when multiple users attempt to modify values simultaneously.
---@field Status aws.connect.DataTableStatus|string The status of the data table. One of PUBLISHED or SAVED. Required parameter that determines the initial state of the table.
---@field Tags? aws.connect.TagMap Key value pairs for attribute based access control (TBAC or ABAC). Optional tags to apply to the data table for organization and access control purposes.

