---Represents a data table in Amazon Connect. A data table is a JSON-like data structure where attributes and values are dynamically set by customers. Customers can reference table values within call flows, applications, views, and workspaces to pinpoint dynamic configuration that changes their contact center's behavior in a predetermined and safe way.
---@class aws.connect.DataTable
---@field Name aws.connect.DataTableName The human-readable name of the data table. Must be unique within the instance and conform to Connect naming standards.
---@field Id aws.connect.DataTableId The unique identifier for the data table. Does not include version aliases.
---@field Arn aws.connect.ARN The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the data table. Does not include version aliases.
---@field TimeZone aws.connect.TimeZone The IANA timezone identifier used when resolving time based dynamic values. Required even if no time slices are specified.
---@field Description? aws.connect.DataTableDescription An optional description of the data table's purpose and contents.
---@field ValueLockLevel? aws.connect.DataTableLockLevel The data level that concurrent value edits are locked on. One of DATA_TABLE, PRIMARY_VALUE, ATTRIBUTE, VALUE, and NONE. Determines how concurrent edits are handled when multiple users attempt to modify values simultaneously.
---@field LockVersion? aws.connect.DataTableLockVersion The lock version information used for optimistic locking and table versioning. Changes with each update to prevent concurrent modification conflicts.
---@field Version? aws.connect.DataTableVersion A unique identifier and alias for customer managed versions (not $LATEST or $SAVED).
---@field VersionDescription? aws.connect.DataTableDescription A description of the customer managed version.
---@field Status? aws.connect.DataTableStatus The current status of the data table. One of PUBLISHED or SAVED.
---@field CreatedTime? aws.connect.Timestamp The timestamp when the data table was created.
---@field LastModifiedTime aws.connect.Timestamp The timestamp when the data table or any of its properties were last modified.
---@field LastModifiedRegion? aws.connect.RegionName The Amazon Web Services Region where the data table was last modified, used for region replication.
---@field Tags? aws.connect.TagMap Key-value pairs for attribute based access control (TBAC or ABAC) and organization.

---A data table access control configuration.
---@class aws.connect.DataTableAccessControlConfiguration
---@field PrimaryAttributeAccessControlConfiguration? aws.connect.PrimaryAttributeAccessControlConfigurationItem The configuration's primary attribute access control configuration.

---Represents an attribute (column) in a data table. Attributes define the schema and validation rules for values that can be stored in the table. They specify the data type, constraints, and whether the attribute is used as a primary key for record identification.
---@class aws.connect.DataTableAttribute
---@field AttributeId? aws.connect.DataTableId The unique identifier for the attribute within the data table.
---@field Name aws.connect.DataTableName The human-readable name of the attribute. Must be unique within the data table and conform to Connect naming standards.
---@field ValueType aws.connect.DataTableAttributeValueType The type of value allowed for this attribute. Must be one of TEXT, TEXT_LIST, NUMBER, NUMBER_LIST, or BOOLEAN. Determines how values are validated and processed.
---@field Description? aws.connect.DataTableDescription An optional description explaining the purpose and usage of this attribute.
---@field DataTableId? aws.connect.DataTableId The unique identifier of the data table that contains this attribute.
---@field DataTableArn? aws.connect.ARN The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the data table that contains this attribute.
---@field Primary aws.connect.Boolean Boolean indicating whether this attribute is used as a primary key for record identification. Primary attributes must have unique value combinations and cannot contain expressions.
---@field Version? aws.connect.DataTableVersion The version identifier for this attribute, used for versioning and change tracking.
---@field LockVersion? aws.connect.DataTableLockVersion The lock version for this attribute, used for optimistic locking to prevent concurrent modification conflicts.
---@field LastModifiedTime? aws.connect.Timestamp The timestamp when this attribute was last modified.
---@field LastModifiedRegion? aws.connect.RegionName The Amazon Web Services Region where this attribute was last modified, used for region replication.
---@field Validation? aws.connect.Validation The validation rules applied to values of this attribute. Based on JSON Schema Draft 2020-12 with additional Connect-specific validations for data integrity.

---@alias aws.connect.DataTableAttributeValueType "TEXT"|"NUMBER"|"BOOLEAN"|"TEXT_LIST"|"NUMBER_LIST"

